# Files listed here are still fully included in every backup -- this
# list only controls whether writing to them, by itself, is allowed to
# schedule a new backup run. A file that's rewritten continuously by
# something else on your machine (a monitoring agent, another app's own
# log) can otherwise keep the watchdog's 300s ceiling firing around the
# clock even with zero real user activity. Add an entry only once you've
# actually confirmed a file behaves this way (e.g. via lsof/stat/
# systemctl on your own machine) -- see rsync_event_handler.py's
# should_ignore(). One pattern per line, same glob syntax as the File
# Exclusions Settings field.
#
# Copy this file to logs/watchdog_trigger_exempt.txt (done automatically
# on first run if it doesn't exist yet) and add your own entries there --
# that file is per-install and never committed, since what needs this
# treatment is specific to your own machine.
#
# Example:
# telegraf.log
